00:14:39,950 --> 00:14:40,150
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

179
00:14:40,710 --> 00:14:46,574
[SPEAKER_02]: But see, if you had kept that knowing there, at that time, you wouldn't have done it.

180
00:14:47,394 --> 00:14:51,077
[SPEAKER_02]: If it was strong enough, if it was strong enough, if it was made

181
00:14:51,988 --> 00:14:55,149
[SPEAKER_02]: On a basis, you wouldn't have engaged in those actions to begin with.

182
00:14:55,169 --> 00:14:55,309
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

183
00:14:55,329 --> 00:14:58,511
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you know it on some level, but it's not about knowing it.

184
00:14:58,851 --> 00:14:58,971
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

185
00:14:59,451 --> 00:15:02,492
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about actively having it present in your mind.

186
00:15:02,512 --> 00:15:02,633
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

187
00:15:03,753 --> 00:15:09,255
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like... And you wouldn't have it present in your mind, because you would ignore it and not frequently bring it up.

188
00:15:09,375 --> 00:15:09,535
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

189
00:15:09,736 --> 00:15:12,537
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like you know you are walking in the minefields.

190
00:15:13,346 --> 00:15:19,050
[SPEAKER_02]: But because you're dealing with this and doing that, you eventually forget that there are places that you shouldn't step on.

191
00:15:19,650 --> 00:15:22,292
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's because you were just not protecting the context.

192
00:15:22,312 --> 00:15:25,734
[SPEAKER_01]: You start overlooking the specific places where you are stepping on.

193
00:15:25,874 --> 00:15:26,074
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

194
00:15:26,734 --> 00:15:30,837
[SPEAKER_01]: Although it's still... it's not not true to say, I know about it.

195
00:15:30,897 --> 00:15:32,838
[SPEAKER_02]: Somebody told you, you would say, yes, of course, I know.

196
00:15:32,918 --> 00:15:33,478
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

197
00:15:33,578 --> 00:15:38,902
[SPEAKER_02]: But in that moment where you get distracted with other things, you're not aware of it.

198
00:15:38,942 --> 00:15:39,142
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

199
00:15:39,222 --> 00:15:42,144
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, so you're not doing this contemplation for some sort of

200
00:15:43,917 --> 00:15:44,958
[SPEAKER_01]: New knowledge or something.

201
00:15:45,198 --> 00:15:50,223
[SPEAKER_01]: It's more like stuff that's... Well, there was kind of almost always self-evident.

202
00:15:51,203 --> 00:15:53,766
[SPEAKER_01]: What's good, what's bad, in a sense.

203
00:15:53,786 --> 00:16:06,176
[SPEAKER_01]: But by actually making a point of sitting down and actively thinking about it, that is something that can be done then, even by somebody who doesn't see the mind.

204
00:16:08,238 --> 00:16:15,686
[SPEAKER_01]: Who still acts out of their duty to do something out of the idea of practice, that would be a right thing to do.

205
00:16:15,706 --> 00:16:17,627
[SPEAKER_01]: That wouldn't be as misguided.

206
00:16:19,189 --> 00:16:22,092
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and then, automatically, if you did that properly...

207
00:16:22,925 --> 00:16:28,347
[SPEAKER_02]: It would start becoming apparent how redundant all the other practices would have been.

208
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:33,349
[SPEAKER_02]: Because it wouldn't have ever revealed these things to you and the fact that you'd have abstained from them.

209
00:16:33,709 --> 00:16:37,110
[SPEAKER_02]: You would just hope that that's going to be resolved on its own if I just double down on this.

210
00:16:39,411 --> 00:16:41,072
[SPEAKER_02]: So you would just like...

211
00:16:41,092 --> 00:16:50,135
[SPEAKER_02]: It's like doing some kind of voodoo dance to stop the fire, while on the side you're just throwing fuel at it still.

212
00:16:51,673 --> 00:16:51,853
[SPEAKER_01]: What?

213
00:16:52,053 --> 00:16:54,914
[SPEAKER_01]: You're dancing, choosing to go and stand in the fire and dance there.

214
00:16:55,875 --> 00:16:58,356
[SPEAKER_01]: So you become the fuel.

215
00:16:58,376 --> 00:17:06,639
[SPEAKER_00]: It's also how you wouldn't become dependent even on that.

216
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:10,761
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's how you hesitated at the beginning, to even say something.

217
00:17:11,401 --> 00:17:12,842
[SPEAKER_00]: Because whatever you would say,

218
00:17:13,921 --> 00:17:25,645
[SPEAKER_00]: ...would fill that space, that would be a barrier between you and that mind, pressuring you to do something, which was the original difficulty.

219
00:17:25,665 --> 00:17:27,786
[SPEAKER_02]: But then your emphasis would start to shift.

220
00:17:28,066 --> 00:17:33,808
[SPEAKER_02]: There are these things that I shouldn't do, rather than, like, I need to keep doing it.

221
00:17:33,848 --> 00:17:38,549
[SPEAKER_00]: Eventually, that would even come to, I need to contemplate what I've been doing during the day.

222
00:17:38,569 --> 00:17:42,451
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and you become aware of that, and Reikunas, that's already a contemplation.

223
00:17:43,635 --> 00:17:54,667
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you could see how even that misguided need that I, you know, described as kind of almost part of that identity of the one who practices, that's what keeps you in touch with the practice.

224
00:17:55,107 --> 00:17:59,852
[SPEAKER_01]: People start... it's like it's real as such, that you can't... yeah, it's wrong, but you can't just stop it.

225
00:18:00,373 --> 00:18:05,338
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you were to, as we describe, as the suttas describe, reflect on your actions,

226
00:18:06,436 --> 00:18:16,998
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, not just in passing, not just once, and then, okay, I know it now, but make a point of whether I know it or not, whether it feels clear, whether it feels redundant, I will still do it.

227
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:20,859
[SPEAKER_01]: I will still bring up questions, self-questioning.

228
00:18:20,959 --> 00:18:21,739
[SPEAKER_01]: Why did I do this?

229
00:18:22,479 --> 00:18:23,180
[SPEAKER_01]: How many times?

230
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:27,340
[SPEAKER_01]: When that compulsion arose, how strong was I?

231
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:28,061
[SPEAKER_01]: How weak was I?

232
00:18:28,541 --> 00:18:29,901
[SPEAKER_01]: Is there a chance for me to not do it?

233
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:37,423
[SPEAKER_01]: Where I'm at, in terms of being overwhelmed by the mind and stuff, could have prevented some of those compulsions.

234
00:18:37,463 --> 00:18:39,865
[SPEAKER_01]: Did they result on account of my other careless choices?

235
00:18:39,885 --> 00:18:41,746
[SPEAKER_01]: They were not necessarily so compulsive and so on.

236
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:52,432
[SPEAKER_01]: Thinking about that will actually, more and more, put even that need to do something mechanically, so to speak, will align it better and make it non-mechanic.

237
00:18:52,792 --> 00:18:59,034
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's just gonna align it with where your intentions are, and then you recognize, well, this is actually what the practice is.

238
00:18:59,054 --> 00:19:14,820
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, and a pattern that you will probably start recognizing pretty soon is, you kind of have these actions that feel like, if you would have really questioned yourself, you would know it's rooted in the wrong intention, but you kind of downplay how bad it is.

239
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,361
[SPEAKER_02]: You think, oh, well, yeah, sure.

240
00:19:17,293 --> 00:19:17,973
[SPEAKER_01]: Think about it later.

241
00:19:17,993 --> 00:19:18,634
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll think about it later.

242
00:19:18,654 --> 00:19:19,334
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll deal with it later.

243
00:19:19,374 --> 00:19:20,395
[SPEAKER_02]: Right now, I need to do this.

244
00:19:20,435 --> 00:19:21,395
[SPEAKER_02]: There's a top priority.

245
00:19:22,016 --> 00:19:27,439
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, you would see, it's because of that, that then, all these other actions become even harder to say no to.

246
00:19:27,459 --> 00:19:28,279
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

247
00:19:28,479 --> 00:19:35,103
[SPEAKER_01]: And when you think about things later, if then remorse comes up, because you recognize, I could...

248
00:19:35,443 --> 00:19:36,584
[SPEAKER_01]: I could have restrained myself.

249
00:19:36,664 --> 00:19:37,605
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't.

250
00:19:39,966 --> 00:19:40,926
[SPEAKER_01]: You allow that remorse.

251
00:19:41,086 --> 00:19:41,227
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

252
00:19:41,427 --> 00:19:41,687
[SPEAKER_01]: That's

253
00:19:44,173 --> 00:19:45,720
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the payment for it, basically.

254
00:19:45,761 --> 00:19:49,237
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how you will strengthen the value for next time, not to do it.

